      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "GOVERNOR"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Governor acts as the nominal executive head (de jure) of the state government.",
        "Appointed by the President of India and holds office during the pleasure of the President.",
        "Must be a citizen of India and at least 35 years of age to qualify for office.",
        "Possesses Executive, Legislative, Financial, and Judicial powers within the state sphere.",
        "Enjoys explicit constitutional discretionary powers distinct from the powers of the President."
      ],
      "id": "dlgo3qi"
    },
